WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.264
In the Southern Dynasties there was a great painter named Zhang Sengyou, whose skill at painting was extraordinarily high.

00:00:06.614 --> 00:00:12.038
One day, he painted four dragons on the wall of a temple — they looked utterly majestic.

00:00:12.388 --> 00:00:16.516
But strangely, none of the four dragons had eyes painted on.

00:00:16.866 --> 00:00:20.298
When someone asked him why, he only smiled and gave no answer.

00:00:20.648 --> 00:00:26.288
Everyone begged him to add the eyes; unable to refuse them, he had no choice but to agree.

00:00:26.638 --> 00:00:30.550
Zhang Sengyou thought for a moment, and at last nodded his head.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.676
He picked up his brush and dotted eyes onto two of the dragons.

00:00:36.026 --> 00:00:39.938
The moment the tip of his brush came down, the sky darkened.

00:00:40.288 --> 00:00:45.232
Suddenly thunder and lightning crashed, and the two dragons actually broke through the wall and flew away!

00:00:45.582 --> 00:00:50.262
The other two dragons, the ones without eyes, remained on the wall.

00:00:50.612 --> 00:00:57.308
From then on, 'dotting the eyes of the painted dragon' became an idiom, describing how one crucial stroke brings a work to life.

